      "id": "q:crm-sync-dupes",
      "question": "When an SDR pushes an Apollo contact into Salesforce or HubSpot, how often does it create a duplicate of a record marketing already owned, and who cleans it up?",
      "why": "This is the pain RevOps would feel most directly, and every description of it I could find was written by competing vendors describing the failure mode rather than by a RevOps practitioner describing their own week. I did not assert it as a pain because I could not source it in buyer voice.",
      "would_change": "A RevOps practitioner describing their own dedupe queue would add an eleventh pain on b2b:ease_of_doing_business:integration, aimed squarely at seg:revops, and would likely rank above pain:click-weight for the mid-market buyer."
    },
    {
