      "question": "What do reps actually say about Apollo's parallel dialer: connect rates, caller ID getting flagged as spam likely, and whether numbers are current?",
      "why": "The parallel dialer is a named feature in brain/company and the dialing motion is half of what an SDR does, but I found no Apollo buyer speaking about it. The general dialer commentary I found was all competing-vendor blog content, which is not evidence about this product.",
      "would_change": "Real rep verbatims would either add a dialer pain around burned caller IDs or confirm the dialer is not where the friction is, which changes which feature to lead with for seg:midmarket."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:bounce-rate-truth",
      "question": "What hard-bounce rate do teams actually see on Apollo exports they did not independently re-verify, measured on their own sends?",
      "why": "Buyers consistently say data is stale, but every specific bounce percentage I encountered traced back to a competing vendor's test or an unsourced summary. Apollo buyers say 'some emails bounce', not a number. A number from a buyer would move pain:bounced-list from qualitative to quantified.",
