  "sources": [
    { "id": "src:1", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "This service is bullshit", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-17", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "This service is bullshit. I am told multiple times by the AI: The real reason it's showing 0 added is most likely that Apollo requires at least one of the following to save a contact: email, phone number, or LinkedIn URL. Your file doesn't have any of those, so Apollo can't anchor the record. Like what? Isn't that the primary value of the platform? I've spent hours going in circles with this thing. No way to share feedback directly, so I'm venting here. Buyer beware." },
    { "id": "src:2", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "Ease of Use", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-16", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Apollo is a great service for small business owners and is relatively easy to use, especially for prospecting and outreach. The main drawback we've experienced is the low response rate to email campaigns, which can make it difficult to determine how effective the outreach is, despite having access to a strong database of contacts." },
    { "id": "src:3", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "Love the platform and the demo", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-16", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Love the platform and the demo. Getting started (specifically linking mailboxes and warming up emails) was another matter. I went through several support agents all who told me that engineering would have to get involved. I finally connected with Valeria who helped me link and warm up the emails. There is nothing intuitive in the set up and I have worked in technology for years. Onboarding process needs better training/instruction." },
    { "id": "src:4", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "A powerful tool with a significant weakness", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-15", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Its a very powerful outreach and inbound tool. The amount of data that you can acquire through Apollo is great! However, I feel the structure of how you are supposed to use it (massmail and outreaches, generic AI slop, etc.) is very tailored to the North American Consumer market whereas for other regions such as Europe or Asia-Pacific this type of approach does not really work. So if you have mainly U.S. clients you should definitely consider using Apollo, if you are elsewhere there might be better options available for you." },
    { "id": "src:5", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "Same bloatware as Salesforce and…", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-14", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Same bloatware as Salesforce and Hubspot, useless search and AI assistant, non-existent support - you are sent to read tons of docs whenever you have a simple question. Load of toggles and buttons with no clear purpose make it impossible to figure out is your warmup all set or you need to keep on reading instructions." },
    { "id": "src:6", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "Extremely expensive and junk data", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-30", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Extremely expensive and most of the data is terrible and invalid...Charges you credits for any action you take inside which makes no sense because you've already paid an arm and a leg for the subscription. Just a money grab on old outdated and junk data" },
    { "id": "src:7", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "Throttling and limits make it unusable", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-27", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Throttling and limits on their free plan makes it unusable and their paid plan is ridiculously expensive. Even their paid basic plan is heavily throttled and restricted." },
    { "id": "src:8", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "Permanently locked out of my account", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-03", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Permanently locked out of my account and no way of getting back in with the value of credits on the account being very substancial. The customer service rep Gustavo Cabrera was no help. I see value in the product but it's completely useless when you get locked out of your account... stay clear." },
    { "id": "src:9", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "UX is very poor compared to other alternatives", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-03", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Data is fine.. but UX is very bad.. heavy loading pages to many windows with slow loading, too many clicks to reach data many navigation buttons seems to be not in the logical place" },
    { "id": "src:10", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "Occasionally the user session closes unexpectedly", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-01-19", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Occasionally the user session closes unexpectedly, and we do not have 100% of the required information, especially email addresses and phone numbers. This has hindered progress with several companies" },
    { "id": "src:11", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?page=4", "title": "Jake Straface, 1-star review", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-11", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "It's utterly impossible to send emails... The damn thing adds all 700 at once and sends them, and then won't let me deactivate... then takes the 25 I wanted to send, only sends 2, and then schedules the other 23 for a undisclosed time." },
    { "id": "src:12", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?page=4", "title": "Shane, 1-star review", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-13", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "This ai system is supposed to send emails for you... However, it failed over and over and over again... It's buggy. It does NOT work." },
    { "id": "src:13", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/", "title": "Ankita P, Business Development Executive, IT and Services", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-09", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "contact data wasn't always accurate or up to date" },
    { "id": "src:14", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews?page=3", "title": "Ellie A, Co-Founder, Computer Software", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-05-16", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "data is not perfect ... some emails can bounce or be missing" },
    { "id": "src:15", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/", "title": "Jordan V, Sales Specialist, Computer Software", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-05-15", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "have to stay organized with your credits to maximize value" },
    { "id": "src:16", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/?sort=lowest_rating", "title": "Abhishek Y, Database Executive, Marketing and Advertising", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-20", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Some contact information is outdated and credit can runs out quickly with heavy" },
    { "id": "src:17", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews?page=3", "title": "Zaro D, Owner, Construction", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-07-15", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "ui and experience is overwhelming" },
    { "id": "src:18", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/?sort=lowest_rating", "title": "Rafay A, Research Staff, Staffing and Recruiting", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-01-08", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Unclear pricing, forced waterfall verification, slow email access" },
    { "id": "src:19", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47649117", "title": "fontain, comment on 'Someone at BrowserStack is leaking users' email addresses'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-04-05", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Apollo's customer data sharing adds any information BrowserStack send to Apollo to the person's profile with Apollo, accessible to all Apollo customers. For example, any other Apollo customer can search something like \"email addresses for decision makers at Example, Inc.\" and get back a list including your email address (if you told BrowserStack you are a decision maker at Example, Inc.) Every single marketing team is doing all of this, the only reason it was obvious in this case is that the OP used a unique email address for BrowserStack." },
    { "id": "src:20", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47649117", "title": "streblo, comment on 'Someone at BrowserStack is leaking users' email addresses'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-04-05", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Everyone in this thread suggesting a \"data leak\" or \"compromise\" is totally missing the fact that this is how Apollo works. This is often times overlooked by Apollo customers themselves. You have to opt out of customer data sharing (and in doing so lose out on the value of the product)" },
    { "id": "src:21", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47649117", "title": "andrewaylett, comment on 'Someone at BrowserStack is leaking users' email addresses'", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-04-05", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "yes, if you have a CRM in then you might derive legitimate interests in sharing with Apollo. But you need to make sure you actually have the right legal basis for putting customer details into your CRM, and your support database almost certainly does not hold appropriate data! So ultimately I think this is on both Browserstack (for connecting and sharing data other than in accordance with a legal basis) and Apollo (for making it too easy for their customers to send them data without a sound legal basis and then for sharing that data without suitably validating they had the legal basis to)." },
    { "id": "src:22", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44504699", "title": "throwaway_323, comment on subscription cancellation rules", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2025-07-09", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Scammy companies like apollo.io follow dark patterns to provide several hoops before cancellation, refuse refunds and one click subscribe into an absurd annual contract. This nullification does not serve the best interest of consumers unfortunately." },
    { "id": "src:23", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=42380054", "title": "jameslk, comment on sales engagement products", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2024-12-10", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "There's a ton of leads agencies that gobble these up sending out tens of thousands of emails every day using the latest incarnation of this spamware, creating new domains and warming them up with fake emails to each other and now using LLMs to \"personalize\" the emails (i.e. the \"AI\") all in the attempt to evade spam filters. There's a new one every day because the last one got banned/isn't effective anymore." },
    { "id": "src:24", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44501076", "title": "constantinum, comment on GTM data tooling", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2025-07-08", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Tools like Clay and Apollo are often misused for spammy cold outreach—which rarely works. The real value lies in enriching leads who've already shown interest, helping align marketing efforts with the right prospects. Beyond that, more data doesn't always improve GTM decisions." },
    { "id": "src:25", "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47649117", "title": "x0x0, comment on how contact data vendors acquire data", "venue": "Hacker News", "speaker": "practitioner", "published": "2026-04-05", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Another way these companies get data is they have credits. It costs a credit for a salesperson to enrich the data of someone they're trying to contact. There are 2 ways to gain credits: 1 - cash; 2 - the salesperson installs a plugin in their inbox and it scrapes all contact info in the inbox." },
    { "id": "src:26", "url": "https://salesmotion.io/blog/apollo-pricing", "title": "Apollo.io Pricing Breakdown 2026: Plans, Credits, and Real Costs", "venue": "Salesmotion blog", "speaker": "vendor", "published": "2026-05", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Credits expire at the end of your billing cycle...Unused credits are forfeited with no refund or extension. Seat reductions are also not permitted mid-contract. Annual contract for best pricing; 30-day cancellation notice; no mid-term seat reductions" },
    { "id": "src:28", "url": "https://www.lusha.com/blog/b2b-data-decay-rate-measured/", "title": "B2B Data Decay Rate: We Measured 12.6% a Year", "venue": "Lusha blog", "speaker": "vendor", "published": "2026-09", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "12.25% changed roles over twelve months ... 25.67% over twenty four. For a defined cohort, a department, a seniority band, a country, we counted the total population, then counted how many of those contacts have an employment change recorded within a given window. The ratio is the job change rate." },
    { "id": "src:29", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "AVOID. Steals and sells your data", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-01", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Steals and sells your data without consent. You get bombarded with junk email. They claim to remove your details but don't at all. Sham of an organisation!" },
    { "id": "src:30", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "it's very useful for my needs", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-09-02", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "I'll be honest, I dont like the absence of results, I do appreciate that the app does not falsify dat. At least To get me some data even if its not the decision maker, something to start with" },
    { "id": "src:32", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io?stars=1&stars=2", "title": "Permanent ban", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-08-28", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "the process was rigid, opaque, and deeply dismissive of a business user's legitimate concerns." },
    { "id": "src:34", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/?sort=lowest_rating", "title": "Sanket D, Media Buyer Manager, Marketing and Advertising", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2026-04-10", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "UI can feel slightly cluttered, and initial setup takes some time" },
    { "id": "src:35", "url": "https://www.capterra.com/p/158696/Apollo/reviews/?sort=lowest_rating", "title": "ryan p, Owner, Design", "venue": "Capterra", "speaker": "buyer", "published": "2025-10-31", "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "interface can feel a bit overwhelming at first" },
    { "id": "src:36", "url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/review/apollo.io", "title": "Apollo.io Reviews, overall score", "venue": "Trustpilot", "speaker": "press", "published": null, "pulled": "2026-09-18", "verbatim": "Overall TrustScore: 3.1/5 (1,315 reviews) | 46% five-star, 36% one-star ratings" },
